<title>GERMANY: Delors-jobs policy a matter for individual states.</title>
<headline>Delors-jobs policy a matter for individual states.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The former president of the European Commission, Jacques Delors, said on Thursday that formulating job market policy was principally a matter for individual European states, not a pan-European issue.</p>
<p>At the same time, Delors said, it made sense for EU states to combine forces to help defeat unemployment.</p>
<p>Speaking on German television, Delors went on to say that the newly-elected French prime minister Jacques Delors did not believe that a higher budget deficit would help him tackle unemployment in France.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
